{
  "schema": 1,
  "about": "The one surface map of agent/plans/PLAN-tested-on-bench.md Design item 2, read only through rediacc_ci.proof.surfaces. Globs are console-relative in the Owns grammar (wl_planconc.normalize_owns, then glob_regex). A surface with a glob under a submodule lives in that submodule; its gitlink pointer joins the inputs digest.",
  "submodules": ["private/renet", "private/account"],
  "surfaces": {
    "renet": {
      "globs": [
        "private/renet/cmd/**",
        "private/renet/pkg/**",
        "private/renet/proxy/**",
        "private/renet/build.sh",
        "private/renet/scripts/pull-with-retry.sh",
        "private/renet/go.mod",
        "private/renet/go.sum",
        "private/renet/embed-assets.lock.json"
      ],
      "live": ["hostinger"],
      "renet_build": true
    },
    "cli-remote": {
      "globs": [
        "packages/cli/src/remote/**",
        "packages/cli/src/services/repo/repo-key-deployment.ts"
      ],
      "live": ["hostinger"],
      "renet_build": true
    },
    "cli": {
      "globs": ["packages/cli/src/**"],
      "live": ["bench", "hostinger"],
      "renet_build": false
    },
    "account": {
      "globs": [
        "private/account/{src,web,drizzle,scripts}/**",
        "private/account/{package.json,package-lock.json,tsconfig.json,wrangler*.toml,dev.defaults.env,docker-compose.yml,Dockerfile}",
        "packages/shared/src/**"
      ],
      "live": ["bench"],
      "renet_build": false
    },
    "account-worker": {
      "globs": ["workers/account/**"],
      "live": ["bench"],
      "renet_build": false
    },
    "proxy": {
      "globs": ["workers/proxy/src/**", "workers/proxy/wrangler*.toml", "workers/proxy/Dockerfile"],
      "live": ["bench"],
      "renet_build": false
    },
    "www": {
      "globs": ["packages/www/src/**", "workers/www/**"],
      "live": ["bench"],
      "renet_build": false
    }
  },
  "exclude": [
    "**/*_test.go",
    "**/*.test.ts",
    "**/*.test.tsx",
    "**/*.spec.ts",
    "**/*.spec.tsx",
    "**/__tests__/**",
    "**/testdata/**",
    "**/tests/**",
    "**/e2e/**",
    "**/*.md",
    "**/.naturalized-hashes.json"
  ],
  "tiers": {
    "vm": {
      "phases": {
        "renet": {"surfaces": ["renet", "cli-remote"]},
        "account": {"surfaces": ["account"]}
      },
      "instrument": {
        ".ci/rediacc_ci/drills/license.py": ["account"],
        ".ci/rediacc_ci/drills/universe.py": ["account"],
        ".ci/rediacc_ci/drills/transfer.py": ["account"],
        ".ci/rediacc_ci/drills/vm_check.py": ["renet", "account"],
        ".ci/rediacc_ci/drills/lib.py": ["renet", "account"],
        ".ci/rediacc_ci/drills/upgrade_converge.py": ["renet"],
        ".ci/rediacc_ci/drills/tenant_isolation.py": ["renet"],
        ".ci/rediacc_ci/drills/session_teardown.py": ["renet"],
        ".ci/rediacc_ci/drills/converge_preflight.py": ["renet"],
        ".ci/rediacc_ci/drills/gpu_grants.py": ["renet"],
        ".ci/rediacc_ci/drills/vm_ssh.py": ["renet", "account"],
        ".ci/rediacc_ci/drills/wire.py": ["renet", "account"],
        ".ci/rediacc_ci/drills/backup_check_trigger.py": ["renet"]
      },
      "areas_about": [
        "agent/plans/PLAN-renet-change-test-triggers.md Design item 3, the one area map.",
        "An area names renet globs (inside the renet surface), the legs that prove a change there, the e2e suites that exercise it and the CI VM jobs that run them.",
        "vm:check computes the touched areas from the same diff as its sides; it RUNS a `vmcheck` leg (step ids of its own battery on its worker fleet), JUDGES a `receipt` leg by the named receipt, and RUNS an `external` leg (an e2e suite on a fleet of its own) after the base battery: it tears its forks down, reuses the fleet when every ip runs or brings it up from `up` (only the `[VAR=value ...] ./rdc.sh ops up [flags]` shape is runnable; a prose recipe is NOT_VERIFIED), runs `cmd` from the console root, judges the last command by its exit code and per-test results, and recreates the vmcheck-base grand when the suite's setup removed it.",
        "A failed test of an external leg makes the run FAILED; any other leg not proven makes it NOT_VERIFIED `area-not-verified`, naming its fleet and its exact commands. A renet runtime path in no area gets the renet base battery alone.",
        ".ci/scripts/ci/scope-map.cjs reads `globs`, `ci_jobs` and the top-level `exclude`: an expanded renet path selects only its areas' VM jobs, and the bare gitlink or a renet path in no area selects them all.",
        "The `exclude` list (test files, docs) is the VM tier's: a test-only renet change needs no VM proof and no CI VM job, and its Go tests are the renet test map's receipt (.ci/config/renet-test-map.json), not this file's."
      ],
      "fleets": {
        "worker": {
          "ips": ["192.168.111.1", "192.168.111.11"],
          "up": "./rdc.sh ops up --basic"
        },
        "two-workers": {
          "ips": ["192.168.111.1", "192.168.111.11", "192.168.111.12"],
          "up": "./rdc.sh ops up"
        },
        "ceph": {
          "ips": ["192.168.111.1", "192.168.111.21", "192.168.111.22", "192.168.111.23"],
          "up": "VM_WORKERS='11 12' VM_CEPH_NODES='21 22 23' ./rdc.sh ops up"
        },
        "ceph-workers": {
          "ips": ["192.168.111.1", "192.168.111.11", "192.168.111.12", "192.168.111.21", "192.168.111.22"],
          "up": "VM_WORKERS='11 12' VM_CEPH_NODES='21 22 23' ./rdc.sh ops up"
        },
        "k3s-ceph": {
          "ips": ["192.168.111.1", "192.168.111.11", "192.168.111.12", "192.168.111.21", "192.168.111.22", "192.168.111.23"],
          "up": "VM_WORKERS='11 12' VM_CEPH_NODES='21 22 23' ./rdc.sh ops up"
        },
        "second-group": {
          "ips": ["192.168.111.1", "192.168.111.11", "192.168.112.5", "192.168.112.51"],
          "up": "./rdc.sh ops up --basic, then group B as ct-tests.yml 'Boot second KVM group (B)' does: VM_NET=renet12 VM_NET_BASE=192.168.112 VM_NET_OFFSET=0 VM_BRIDGE=5 VM_WORKERS=51 VM_CEPH_NODES='' PROVISION_CEPH_CLUSTER=false private/renet/bin/renet ops up --force --parallel"
        }
      },
      "areas": {
        "license": {
          "what": "the licence store, tier map, renewal and presence checks renet enforces per repository",
          "globs": [
            "private/renet/pkg/license/**",
            "private/renet/pkg/subscription/**",
            "private/renet/cmd/renet/license_*.go",
            "private/renet/cmd/renet/repository_license_*.go",
            "private/renet/cmd/renet/backup_license.go"
          ],
          "legs": [
            {"id": "license-drill", "kind": "vmcheck", "steps": ["A0", "A2.3"], "what": "the license drill, legs c,d,e,f (renewal from a credential-less machine, refusal on a lapsed subscription, soft claim over cap, the DTO boundary), on the worker against the dev gateway A0 starts"}
          ],
          "suites": [
            "packages/e2e-tests/tests/04-repository-lifecycle.test.ts",
            "packages/e2e-tests/tests/13-postgres-fork-isolation.test.ts",
            "packages/e2e-tests/tests/kube/24-cluster-licensing.test.ts"
          ],
          "ci_jobs": ["e2e_workers", "fork_isolation"]
        },
        "functions": {
          "what": "the function registry and executor behind `renet execute`, which every rdc repo verb dispatches through",
          "globs": [
            "private/renet/pkg/functions/*.go",
            "private/renet/pkg/functions/{commands,compatibility,progress,provider,vault}/**",
            "private/renet/cmd/renet/{functions_commands,execute_command}.go"
          ],
          "legs": [
            {"id": "execute-path", "kind": "vmcheck", "steps": ["P5", "V1.1", "U1"], "what": "repo create, fork and converge on the worker, each through `renet execute`"}
          ],
          "suites": [
            "packages/e2e-tests/tests/03-datastore-lifecycle.test.ts",
            "packages/e2e-tests/tests/04-repository-lifecycle.test.ts",
            "packages/e2e-tests/tests/05-rediaccfiles-updown.test.ts",
            "packages/e2e-tests/tests/06-daemon-operations.test.ts",
            "packages/e2e-tests/tests/07-container-operations.test.ts"
          ],
          "ci_jobs": ["e2e_workers", "fork_isolation"]
        },
        "migrate": {
          "what": "repository migration between machines and between KVM groups, and the cross-group mesh it rides",
          "globs": [
            "private/renet/cmd/renet/repository_migrate*.go",
            "private/renet/pkg/functions/commands/repository_migrate.go",
            "private/renet/pkg/infra/mesh/**"
          ],
          "legs": [
            {
              "id": "cli-migrate-23",
              "kind": "external",
              "fleet": "two-workers",
              "what": "suite 23, rdc-driven repo migrate routing across two workers",
              "cmd": [
                "PYTHONPATH=.ci python3 -m rediacc_ci.env.create_e2e_env --renet-path \"$PWD/private/renet/bin/renet\" --output packages/e2e-tests/.env --vm-workers \"11 12\"",
                "BRIDGE_TEST_SKIP_RESET=1 PYTHONPATH=.ci python3 -m rediacc_ci.testrun.e2e --workers 1 --test 23-cli-migrate-routing --fail-on-skip"
              ]
            },
            {
              "id": "dual-group-18",
              "kind": "external",
              "fleet": "second-group",
              "what": "suite 18, a migrate from group A to a second KVM group B (the e2e_migrate job)",
              "cmd": [
                "PYTHONPATH=.ci python3 -m rediacc_ci.env.create_e2e_env --renet-path \"$PWD/private/renet/bin/renet\" --output packages/e2e-tests/.env --vm-workers \"11\" --vm-ram-worker 4096 --k8s",
                "PYTHONPATH=.ci python3 -m rediacc_ci.testrun.e2e --workers 1 --config playwright.migrate.config.ts --fail-on-skip"
              ]
            }
          ],
          "suites": [
            "packages/e2e-tests/tests/migrate/18-dual-group-migrate.test.ts",
            "packages/e2e-tests/tests/23-cli-migrate-routing.test.ts"
          ],
          "ci_jobs": ["e2e_migrate", "e2e_workers"]
        },
        "multi-vm": {
          "what": "operations spanning two workers: machine-to-machine push and pull, the SSH layer and the orchestration workflows",
          "globs": [
            "private/renet/pkg/ssh/**",
            "private/renet/pkg/orchestration/**",
            "private/renet/pkg/infra/mesh/**",
            "private/renet/cmd/renet/backup_{push,pull}*.go"
          ],
          "legs": [
            {
              "id": "multi-machine-11",
              "kind": "external",
              "fleet": "two-workers",
              "what": "suite 11, connectivity, setup, push/pull and parallel execution across workers .11 and .12",
              "cmd": [
                "PYTHONPATH=.ci python3 -m rediacc_ci.env.create_e2e_env --renet-path \"$PWD/private/renet/bin/renet\" --output packages/e2e-tests/.env --vm-workers \"11 12\"",
                "BRIDGE_TEST_SKIP_RESET=1 PYTHONPATH=.ci python3 -m rediacc_ci.testrun.e2e --workers 1 --test 11-multi-machine --fail-on-skip"
              ]
            }
          ],
          "suites": [
            "packages/e2e-tests/tests/11-multi-machine.test.ts",
            "packages/e2e-tests/tests/12d-full-integration-multi-machine.test.ts"
          ],
          "ci_jobs": ["e2e_workers"]
        },
        "ceph": {
          "what": "RBD-backed datastores, Ceph cluster provisioning and the ceph functions",
          "globs": [
            "private/renet/pkg/rbd/**",
            "private/renet/pkg/infra/{ceph,cephpkg}/**",
            "private/renet/pkg/toolexec/ceph/**",
            "private/renet/cmd/renet/ceph*.go",
            "private/renet/cmd/renet/ops_{ceph,up_ceph_mirror}.go",
            "private/renet/pkg/functions/commands/ceph.go"
          ],
          "legs": [
            {
              "id": "ceph-08-09-12c",
              "kind": "external",
              "fleet": "ceph",
              "what": "the e2e_ceph job: pool and image, snapshot and clone, full integration on the Ceph trio",
              "cmd": [
                "PYTHONPATH=.ci python3 -m rediacc_ci.env.create_e2e_env --ceph --renet-path \"$PWD/private/renet/bin/renet\" --output packages/e2e-tests/.env",
                "PYTHONPATH=.ci python3 -m rediacc_ci.testrun.e2e --workers 1 --config playwright.ceph.config.ts --fail-on-skip"
              ]
            },
            {
              "id": "ceph-workers-13-14",
              "kind": "external",
              "fleet": "ceph-workers",
              "what": "the e2e_ceph_workers job: a Ceph datastore and multiple clients on the workers",
              "cmd": [
                "PYTHONPATH=.ci python3 -m rediacc_ci.env.create_e2e_env --renet-path \"$PWD/private/renet/bin/renet\" --output packages/e2e-tests/.env --vm-workers \"11 12\" --vm-ceph-nodes \"21 22\" --vm-ram-worker 2560 --vm-ram-ceph 2560",
                "PYTHONPATH=.ci python3 -m rediacc_ci.testrun.e2e --workers 1 --config playwright.ceph-workers.config.ts --fail-on-skip"
              ]
            }
          ],
          "suites": [
            "packages/e2e-tests/tests/ceph/08-ceph-pool-image.test.ts",
            "packages/e2e-tests/tests/ceph/09-ceph-snapshot-clone.test.ts",
            "packages/e2e-tests/tests/ceph/12c-full-integration-ceph.test.ts",
            "packages/e2e-tests/tests/ceph/13-ceph-datastore.test.ts",
            "packages/e2e-tests/tests/ceph/14-ceph-multiclient.test.ts"
          ],
          "ci_jobs": ["e2e_ceph", "e2e_ceph_workers", "e2e_k8s_ceph"]
        },
        "kube": {
          "what": "k8s repositories: the k3s runtime inside a repo, the CSI driver, kube volumes and multinode clusters",
          "globs": [
            "private/renet/pkg/{kube,kubecsi,kubevolume}/**",
            "private/renet/cmd/renet/kube*.go",
            "private/renet/cmd/renet/repository_fork_kube.go",
            "private/renet/pkg/functions/commands/kube*.go",
            "private/renet/pkg/reporuntime/kube*.go",
            "private/renet/pkg/nodeteardown/**"
          ],
          "legs": [
            {
              "id": "k8s-15",
              "kind": "external",
              "fleet": "worker",
              "what": "the e2e_k8s job: a k8s repo running k3s inside a datastore-backed image on one worker",
              "cmd": [
                "PYTHONPATH=.ci python3 -m rediacc_ci.env.create_e2e_env --renet-path \"$PWD/private/renet/bin/renet\" --output packages/e2e-tests/.env --vm-workers \"11\" --vm-ram-worker 4096",
                "PYTHONPATH=.ci python3 -m rediacc_ci.testrun.e2e --workers 1 --config playwright.k8s.config.ts --fail-on-skip"
              ]
            },
            {
              "id": "k8s-ceph-16",
              "kind": "external",
              "fleet": "k3s-ceph",
              "what": "the e2e_k8s_ceph job: a datastore cluster on Ceph",
              "cmd": [
                "PYTHONPATH=.ci python3 -m rediacc_ci.env.create_e2e_env --renet-path \"$PWD/private/renet/bin/renet\" --output packages/e2e-tests/.env --vm-workers \"11 12\" --vm-ceph-nodes \"21 22 23\" --vm-ram-worker 3072 --vm-ram-ceph 2560",
                "PYTHONPATH=.ci python3 -m rediacc_ci.testrun.e2e --workers 1 --config playwright.k8s-ceph.config.ts --fail-on-skip"
              ]
            },
            {
              "id": "k8s-multinode-17-24",
              "kind": "external",
              "fleet": "k3s-ceph",
              "what": "the e2e_k8s_multinode job: a multinode cluster, and suite 24's cluster licensing (CLUSTER_LICENSING_SUITE=1)",
              "cmd": [
                "PYTHONPATH=.ci python3 -m rediacc_ci.env.create_e2e_env --renet-path \"$PWD/private/renet/bin/renet\" --output packages/e2e-tests/.env --vm-workers \"11 12\" --vm-ceph-nodes \"21 22 23\" --vm-ram-worker 3072 --vm-ram-ceph 2560",
                "CLUSTER_LICENSING_SUITE=1 PYTHONPATH=.ci python3 -m rediacc_ci.testrun.e2e --workers 1 --config playwright.k8s-multinode.config.ts --fail-on-skip"
              ]
            }
          ],
          "suites": [
            "packages/e2e-tests/tests/kube/15-k8s-repo.test.ts",
            "packages/e2e-tests/tests/kube/16-datastore-cluster.test.ts",
            "packages/e2e-tests/tests/kube/17-multinode-cluster.test.ts",
            "packages/e2e-tests/tests/kube/24-cluster-licensing.test.ts"
          ],
          "ci_jobs": ["e2e_k8s", "e2e_k8s_ceph", "e2e_k8s_multinode"]
        },
        "backup": {
          "what": "the chunk store, snapshot, push, pull, restore and prune paths, and the datastore they read",
          "globs": [
            "private/renet/cmd/renet/{backup,datastore,repository_prune,prune_commands}*",
            "private/renet/pkg/{chunkstore,delta,datastore,coldbackup,backupstate,prune,restorepath,bwrate,fiemap,repodiff,snapshot}/**",
            "private/renet/pkg/functions/commands/backup.go"
          ],
          "legs": [
            {
              "id": "backup-drills",
              "kind": "receipt",
              "receipt": "backup-check",
              "what": "the backup drills' VERIFIED receipt for this tree (rediacc_ci.drills.backup_check_trigger.admit, the receipt block_backup_unverified_push reads)",
              "cmd": ["./run.sh drill backup", "./run.sh drill backup-onprem"]
            }
          ],
          "suites": [
            "packages/e2e-tests/tests/10-backup-checkpoint.test.ts",
            "packages/e2e-tests/tests/15-storage-backup.test.ts",
            "packages/e2e-tests/tests/25-backup-chunk-store.test.ts",
            "packages/e2e-tests/tests/26-backup-storage-cli.test.ts",
            "packages/e2e-tests/tests/27-backup-browse-at.test.ts"
          ],
          "ci_jobs": ["e2e_workers", "e2e_backup_browse_at"]
        }
      }
    },
    "live": {
      "baseline_at": "2026-10-28",
      "targets": {
        "bench": {"origin_wk": "WK_BENCH_ORIGIN"},
        "hostinger": {"config": "eu-bench", "machines": ["hostinger"]}
      },
      "checks": {
        "account-smoke": {
          "targets": ["bench"],
          "surfaces": ["account", "account-worker"],
          "deploy": "bench-cache",
          "what": "the bench account Worker answers /health and /.well-known/server-info; the version recorded by deploy_bench is the one serving 100% at check time",
          "steps": [
            {"id": "health", "argv": ["curl", "-fsS", "--max-time", "30", "{origin}/account/api/v1/health"]},
            {"id": "server-info", "argv": ["curl", "-fsS", "--max-time", "30", "{origin}/account/api/v1/.well-known/server-info"]}
          ]
        },
        "proxy-ready": {
          "targets": ["bench"],
          "surfaces": ["proxy"],
          "deploy": "unrecorded",
          "what": "deploy_proxy --smoke-only against bench: /v1/health 200, /v1/server-info 401 and /v1/ready on the newest deployment; no deploy record ties that version to a console head yet, so a run is NOT_VERIFIED not-live",
          "steps": [
            {"id": "smoke", "argv": ["python3", "-m", "rediacc_ci.deploy.deploy_proxy", "--target", "bench", "--smoke-only"], "timeout_s": 900}
          ]
        },
        "cli-bench": {
          "targets": ["bench"],
          "surfaces": ["cli"],
          "deploy": "tree",
          "what": "the CLI built from the clean head tree reads its subscription from the bench account server through the eu-bench config",
          "steps": [
            {"id": "subscription", "argv": ["./rdc.sh", "--config", "eu-bench", "subscription", "status"]}
          ]
        },
        "www-smoke": {
          "targets": ["bench"],
          "surfaces": ["www"],
          "deploy": "unrecorded",
          "what": "no bench www Worker exists yet (workers/www carries wrangler.toml and wrangler.edge.toml only), so no deploy identity ties a served version to a console head: every run is NOT_VERIFIED not-live and writes no row; it meets LP7's coverage rule and cannot close a box until a bench www deploy is recorded",
          "steps": [
            {"id": "root", "argv": ["curl", "-fsS", "--max-time", "30", "{origin}/"]}
          ]
        },
        "renet-live": {
          "targets": ["hostinger"],
          "surfaces": ["renet", "cli-remote", "cli"],
          "deploy": "renet-hash",
          "per_machine": true,
          "rebuild": ["./rdc.sh", "--version"],
          "what": "per machine alias: bin/renet is the renet pointer unmodified (rebuilt once), machine status provisions it and reports stale_binary empty, and the remote renet hash equals the local sha256",
          "steps": [
            {"id": "status", "expect": "stale-binary-empty", "argv": ["./rdc.sh", "--config", "{config}", "machine", "status", "{machine}", "-o", "json"], "timeout_s": 900},
            {"id": "hash", "expect": "renet-hash", "argv": ["./rdc.sh", "--config", "{config}", "term", "connect", "{machine}", "-c", "/usr/lib/rediacc/renet/current/renet hash"]}
          ]
        }
      },
      "pointer_only": ["private/renet", "private/account"]
    }
  }
}
